      "evidence": "The frozen console receipt flags the correct option as the sole longest in all 18 questions. Whole-option review confirms that each key is a complete multi-clause implementation recipe, while distractors repeatedly use four shorter stock models: publish before validation, delegate the invariant to a consumer, wait for every projection, or broadcast a write command. In several stems the key's owner/validation boundary is already made explicit, so the answer-shape cue can substitute for selecting the event contract.",
      "requiredCorrection": "Revise the affected choice sets coherently with complete, credible competing event contracts and comparable concreteness. Distinguish the wrong models by their actual mistaken boundary or consequence. Avoid filler and equal-length rules; retain IDs where meaning is unchanged."
    }
